comments[5]{created_at,author,text}:
  "2026-11-14T16:55:49.640Z","harness:claude-code","Root cause (2026-11-14): normalizeDirectExtensionCommandOptions in src/sdk/extension/command-options.ts split folded options into declared and passthrough maps and passed every undeclared key straight to the handler; refuseDirectDeclarationViolations threw a bare PmCliError for a missing required flag with no context, so the code was undefined. The CLI path reported missing_required_option only because src/cli/error-guidance.ts derived it from the message text, and that heuristic printed a broken 'Pass ... for extension command ... with a valid value' hint plus pm create examples. Fix: shared refusal helpers with literal codes for both validators (missing_required_option with flag, field = handler key, recovery.missing and a command-specific example; extension_option_disabled; unknown_option), and the direct path refuses any key that is neither a declared spelling nor host-owned (reserved host flags in camel, snake or dashed form, plus the pm_run transport keys force, subcommand, inputResponses and requestState, which reach the same option record). Census before tightening: pm-presets injects resolvedParameterValues inside its own code, not through the host, and pm-linear/pm-presets runtime code makes no direct PmClient.run calls with extra keys."
  "2026-11-14T17:28:40.360Z","harness:claude-code","Bundled-package census before the refusal (2026-11-14): grepped every bundled package's handler reads of context.options and importer options. pm-vcs reads parent and at, both declared; the beads and todos importers read file, backupDir, preserveSourceIds, folder and message, all declared, and author, which is host-owned. pm-calendar's meet, event and remind read inheritFocus without declaring it, so only direct callers could ever set it and the CLI refused --no-inherit-focus as unknown; tests/unit/packages/calendar-shortcuts.spec.ts failed on the new refusal (Unknown option 'inheritFocus' for extension command 'meet'). Fixed by declaring --inherit-focus (boolean, help text shortened to stay inside the flag-help token ratchet) in the package's common flags; on the built CLI pm meet --no-inherit-focus now creates the meeting without the focused parent, which was impossible before."
  "2026-11-14T17:53:02.880Z","harness:claude-code","Codex review round 1 (gpt-6.1-sol xhigh, head 0f221bf98), two P2 findings, both verified and fixed: (1) an extension that extends or overrides a native command (registerFlags('list', ...) plus a list handler) had the native options (all, status) refused for direct callers, because the normalizer saw only contributed flags while CLI dispatch validates contributed and native definitions together. Fix: normalizeDirectExtensionCommandOptions takes nativeDefinitions; the harness and PmClient.run pass resolveNativeCommandOptionDefinitions(commandPath) (new src/sdk/extension/native-command-options.ts, kept out of command-options.ts so the sdk/authoring entrypoint does not load the flag-contract tables); an extension-created path resolves to the shared global flags only. (2) harness read-output admission judged the raw handler result while native formatOutput applies a registered command-result override first; admission now runs on the override's result and skips a suppressed-host-output result (tests/unit/sdk/extension/harness-parity.spec.ts covers both directions)."
  "2026-11-14T18:16:16.016Z","harness:claude-code","Codex review round 2 (head 51f6bd6cd), three P2 findings, all verified and fixed: (1) native aliases (--tags for --tag) and the positive key a --no-* flag sets (truncate from --no-truncate) were still refused for an extension that extends list; resolveNativeCommandOptionDefinitions now admits the canonical flag with its short letter, every alias, and the positive key of each --no-* flag, values untouched. (2) harness read-output admission ignored a structured output_format replacement that native formatEffectiveOutput admits in place of the result; the activation now attaches its service registry to the command registry (symbol pm.sdk.testing.activatedServices) and admission runs output_format first: a structured replacement is admitted, a string rendering leaves the result itself to be admitted. (3) an inline declaration (--from-tracker <path>) leaked its placeholder into flag, recovery.missing and the example (--from-tracker <path> <value>); formatLooseOptionLabel now labels a declaration by resolveExtensionLongFlagName, and the missing-option usage is built from the declared value contract (<path>, [kind] or none). Specs in tests/unit/sdk/extension/harness-parity.spec.ts."
  "2026-11-14T18:49:23.140Z","harness:claude-code","Codex review round 3 (head 72046c9d4), four P2 findings, all verified and fixed: (1) runtime-schema flags (a workspace --story-points on list) were still refused on a native path an extension extends, which showed that enumerating every key a native command accepts (aliases, negations, settings-dependent runtime fields) is open-ended. Decision: the unknown-key refusal applies to extension-created command paths only; on a native path (hasSubcommandFlagContractsForCommand) undeclared keys keep passing through exactly as before, because the native contract owns them. normalizeDirectExtensionCommandOptions takes a DirectExtensionOptionPolicy ({ undeclaredKeys: 'refuse' | 'pass' }) and the harness and PmClient.run pass resolveDirectExtensionOptionPolicy(commandPath); the round-1/2 native-spelling enumeration is removed. GH-1727 is about extension commands, so its acceptance criteria are unaffected. (2) a raw repeatable declaration passed straight to the exported normalizer (no loader) was read as single-value; repeatable now counts as list at entry. (3) the harness ran output_format with the JSON branch even when the caller passed outputFormat: 'toon'; the format now comes from resolveReadOutputEncoding first. (4) the SDK surface snapshot is regenerated with an acknowledgement for the optional trailing policy argument, and DirectExtensionOptionPolicy is exported from ./sdk and ./sdk/authoring."
